  "_readme": "Seed for config/films.json, keyed by the WordPress film id (wp_sspulse_films.id). Copy to config/films.json and fill the blanks. Films 2-4 (Raktdhaar, Dilli Se Dubai, Kaali Raat) are deliberately absent: they are the fictional onboarding examples and must never consume real API quota. WHAT IS ALREADY DONE: title, release_date, industries, and hashtags derived from the title. WHAT YOU MUST FILL, because no connector can resolve it and a wrong value is worse than an empty one: yt_trailer_ids / yt_teaser_ids / yt_song_ids (the id is the v= parameter of a YouTube URL - a wrong id silently feeds another film's views into the forecast), wiki_title (the exact Wikipedia page title, underscores for spaces, e.g. Drishyam_3), and hashtag_account (an ig_user_id from config/assets.json). WHAT RESOLVES ITSELF: tmdb_id and imdb_id are optional - TMDB matches on title plus release year. BUDGET: hashtag search allows 30 unique hashtags per IG account per rolling 7 days, and this file asks for 3 each across 6 films, so spread hashtag_account over at least two of your accounts rather than pointing them all at one.",
